## Safety notes

{safety}

Use `PAPER_CURATION_NO_DEPLOY=1 node ./bin/paper-curation.mjs topic` to list exact valid topic aliases. It reads only `config.json`, never invokes setup, and prints aliases without collection values or credentials. If no valid topic exists, run setup rather than inventing one. Never hardcode example aliases. For local viewing, use `PAPER_CURATION_NO_DEPLOY=1 node ./bin/paper-curation.mjs serve --topic <topic>`; it serves localhost only.

Never expose `.env`, API keys, OAuth tokens, or credential-bearing command lines. For smoke, preview, repair, search/register, and ordinary local curation, keep `PAPER_CURATION_NO_DEPLOY=1`, `PAPER_CURATION_NO_VECTOR_REBUILD=1`, and `--no-deploy`. Deployment scope preview uses only `node ./bin/paper-curation.mjs deploy --topic <topic> --dry-run`; actual deployment is unavailable and fails closed.

Before any provider action, show the provider, model, work, maxima, and cost; obtain fresh approval scoped to that operation. `auto` is OAuth-only. An API key is used only for an explicit approved action. Do not substitute a provider automatically. When Gemini Audio is unavailable, hide and disable it, make zero calls, and keep core curation safe.

Report only observed results: configured topic aliases; authentication mode without credential values; doctor pass, warning, and failure counts; smoke or curation output location; localhost serve address; and the exact deployment preview scope. Never claim a product deployment occurred.
